    "flat": {
      "type": "pln-pdp-flat",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "The question every dog bed gets asked",
        "heading": "Will it go flat?",
        "lede": "<p>Fair question, because it's how most dog beds end: plump in the shop, flat by spring, and a dog sleeping on the floor with a cover over it. So here is what's actually inside the [bed], and what we'll do if it ever lets you down.</p>",
        "core_note": "Foam, not loose filling that packs down.",
        "density_note": "Density, not feel, is what decides whether a foam still holds its shape in month six.",
        "guarantee_text": "If the foam loses its structure under normal use inside [years] years, we replace the foam. Covers, zips and liners wear with use and sit outside it.",
        "threshold_pct": 0,
        "guarantee_text_threshold": "If it loses more than [pct]% of its depth at the centre within [years] years of normal use, we replace the foam. Covers, zips and liners wear with use and sit outside it.",
        "claim_link": "",
        "test_heading": "The hand test, tonight",
        "test_text": "Press a flat hand into the middle of their current bed, where they lie. If you can feel the floor through it, so can their hips and elbows. Do the same on the [bed] whenever you like: if the foam ever fails that test under normal use inside the guarantee, that's exactly what the guarantee is for.",
        "soft_eyebrow": "Straight answer",
        "soft_heading": "Soft, not firm.",
        "soft_text": "<p>The [bed] is a [core] bed: soft to sink into rather than supportive underneath, and it isn't under the foam guarantee. For a dog who gets up stiff, a foam bed will do more for them. For a dog who wants somewhere soft, this is it. The [nights]-night trial applies either way.</p>",
        "foam_label": "See the foam beds",
        "foam_link": "/collections/orthopaedic-dog-beds",
        "layers_heading": "Inside the [bed], top to bottom",
        "image_alt": "",
        "caption": "",
        "tone": "moss"
      }
    },
