    "faq": {
      "type": "pln-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "f1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I know which size to get?",
            "answer": "<p>Measure nose to base of tail while they're lying down, then add about 20cm. Between two sizes? Go up. The size cards above list the sleeping area where we've measured it. Still unsure? Send us their breed and weight.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What size for a Labrador?",
            "answer": "<p>Most adult Labradors need the Large or the XL, and a sprawler needs the bigger of the two. Measure them lying stretched out, nose to base of tail, add about 20cm, and compare with the sleeping area on the size cards. If that lands between two sizes, go up: a bed that's slightly too big is never the problem, one that's too small always is.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it actually be memory foam, or that egg-crate stuff?",
            "answer": "<p>The \"What's inside\" card above says exactly what's in this bed: the core type and, where we've measured it, the depth and the density. If it's memory foam over egg-crate foam, it says so. If it's fibre, it says so. We'd rather you knew now than in month three.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Our last one went flat in a month. How is this different?",
            "answer": "<p>Beds that go flat are usually loose fibre, or thin foam that bottoms out. This one is built on a foam core, listed above with its depth, and the core is guaranteed for [years] years: if it loses its structure under normal use, we replace the foam. Covers, zips and liners wear with use and sit outside the guarantee, which is why we'd rather you had a spare cover than a new bed.</p>",
            "foam_only": true
          }
        },
        "f2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if my dog just won't use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Then it comes back. Put it where they already sleep, with a blanket that smells of home on top. If after a fortnight it still isn't right, tell us any time inside the [nights] nights and we collect it free from the UK mainland and refund every penny.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "He's not a 'bed dog'. He'd rather have the floor.",
            "answer": "<p>A dog who picks the kitchen floor over his bed has usually done the comparison: the floor is flatter and firmer than a bed that has bottomed out. Put the new one where he already sleeps, old blanket on top, and give him a fortnight. If he still won't, it comes back inside the [nights] nights and you're refunded in full.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it help a dog with arthritis or stiff hips?",
            "answer": "<p>Foam spreads their weight so pressure isn't concentrated on hips, elbows and shoulders, and a low front means stepping in rather than climbing over. A bed is for comfort, not a treatment, so please keep talking to your vet.</p>",
            "foam_only": true
          }
        },
        "f10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "She's started having the odd accident. Is it waterproof?",
            "answer": "<p>Where this bed has a waterproof inner liner, it's listed under \"Why the bed\" above, and the liner sits between cover and foam so an accident stops before the core. Where it doesn't, the cover comes off and washes and the <a href=\"/pages/care-guide\">care guide</a> shows how to protect the foam. Either way, a second cover means one is always on the bed.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I wash it?",
            "answer": "<p>Where the cover comes off, it washes following the care label sewn into it. Coated covers wipe clean. Foam is never machine washed. See the <a href=\"/pages/care-guide\">care guide</a>.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it smell when it arrives?",
            "answer": "<p>Foam beds often arrive rolled or vacuum-packed. Unroll it somewhere ventilated and give it a few hours to come back to full depth before they try it. If anything about it isn't right once it has, that's what the [nights] nights are for.</p>",
            "foam_only": true
          }
        },
        "f12": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I really send something this big back?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Inside the [nights] nights, tell us and we arrange collection free from the UK mainland, slept on, hair and all, and refund every penny. You don't need to find a box that fits.</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        },
        "f13": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "It's a lot for a dog bed. Why?",
            "answer": "<p>Dogs spend twelve to fourteen hours a day lying down. Spread over the [years] years the foam is guaranteed for, it comes to the pennies-a-night figure above. Compare that with a bed that's flat by spring, and the one you buy to replace it, and the one after that.</p>",
            "foam_only": true
          }
        },
        "f5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "When will it arrive?",
            "answer": "<p>The dates for an order placed today are above the button. Own stock is dispatched in [dispatch] working days and delivered [transit] working days later. [delivery].</p>",
            "foam_only": false
          }
        }
      },
